Source: ekushe
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ekushe Next <khan.ytube24@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), @RUST@, gcc, g++, make, pkgconf | pkg-config, libibus-1.0-dev, libfcitx5core-dev, libgtk-3-dev, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://ekushenext.com
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/mahbub-khan25/ekushenext
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/mahbub-khan25/ekushenext.git
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ekushe
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, ibus | fcitx5, xdg-utils
Recommends: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0
Provides: ibus-ekushe, fcitx5-ekushe
Description: Bangla phonetic keyboard for IBus and Fcitx 5, with its own dictionary
 Ekushe Next is a Bangla keyboard. Type Bangla the way it sounds in English
 letters (amar sonar bangla -> আমার সোনার বাংলা) and Ekushe writes it with
 Bangla Academy standard spellings, using its own dictionary. Suggestions,
 conjunct hints and Backspace undo are built in. Everything runs on your
 computer; nothing you type is sent anywhere. Works with IBus and with
 Fcitx 5.
 .
 Also includes Ekushe Studio: a writing pad, conjunct guide, spell checker and
 a Bijoy to Unicode converter, in its own window on any desktop (GNOME,
 KDE Plasma, COSMIC, Xfce and others).
